      "message": "Are you sure this was actually a u64 in iOS 3.0/4.0 times? The reason it is u32 is because everything in mach_host (done by by hikari_no_yume) is all natural_t aka u32 and frameworks/foundation.rs NSUInteger aka u32 already existed.\nAlso a u32 can be 4,294,967,295 which if that is bytes it is equivlent to around 4GB, which considering we are assuming physicalMemory is around 2GB, a u32 is fine.\n\nEasy to change this, but different what was done in prior in touchHLE.  Also, what would I call it, just use u64? uint64_t? u_int64_t?\n\nSee https://developer.apple.com/documentation/kernel/uint64_t?changes\u003d_1__8,_1__8\u0026language\u003dobjc,objc\nand\nhttps://developer.apple.com/documentation/kernel/u_int64_t?changes\u003d_1__8,_1__8\u0026language\u003dobjc,objc",
